# Descaling an electric kettle with citric acid

Problem
Limescale (calcium carbonate) builds up on the heating element and walls,
water takes longer to boil, efficiency drops and everything tastes bad.
Citric acid dissolves the scale and is cheap, food-grade and easy to handle.

Materials
citric acid powder (or a descaling tablet), water
plastic or wooden spoon, old towel

Steps
1. fill the kettle about half full with water
2. add 2-3 tablespoons of citric acid (roughly 1 tbsp per litre)
   or one descaling tablet
3. bring to a boil, switch off, let it sit 30-60 min
   (heavily scaled kettles: leave it overnight)
4. pour the solution out and rinse the inside a couple of times
5. fill with clean water, boil once, discard - kills any sour taste
6. wipe and dry, done

